{
  "esm": "1.2.0",
  "metadata": {
    "name": "rates-wear-runspec",
    "description": "PLAN.md §7.3.48: `rates-wear`, the Rates-scale twin of `process-brakewear` and `process-tirewear` together -- brake wear (9) and tire wear (10) PM10 and PM2.5 beside running Total Energy for the gasoline-selected passenger car in Washtenaw County on road type 4, at `<modelscale value=\"Rates\"/>`.\n\nWHAT IT DISCRIMINATES. Brake and tire wear keep the speed bin at Rates scale as running exhaust does (BaseRateGenerator's `useAvgSpeedBin`), so their PM2.5 is the per-bin normalized rate over the bin speed and reproduced with no change. Their PM10 is CHAINED from it by `PM10EmissionRatio`, and MOVES's chained calculators act on BaseRateOutput's emissionRate as they do on a quantity: the ratio is constant across the 16 bins within each cohort (8.0 for brake wear's older model years), so PM10 is the inventory's chain applied to the per-bin rate (`rtRate_chained`). It was zero before §7.3.48.\n\nTHE BINDINGS. `n_ratesScale` = 1 and `n_outputRate` = 625, five pollutant-processes of 125 cohorts, checked by `rateSurvivorCount`.",
    "authors": [
      "EarthSciML Authors and Contributors"
    ],
    "tags": [
      "runspec",
      "onroad",
      "default-database",
      "rates",
      "rates-wear"
    ]
  },
  "data_sources": {
    "db_runspecyear": {
      "kind": "static",
      "source": {
        "url_template": "../../moves.rs/characterization/snapshots/rates-wear/tables/db__movesexecution1ccc0233_campuscluster_illinois_edu__runspecyear.parquet"
      },
      "extent": {
        "metaparameter": "n_runspecyear"
      },
      "metadata": {
        "tags": [
          "scope"
        ],
        "note": "1 row, yearID 2020. The scope comes from these tables and never from the RunSpec XML, whose @key attributes are 0-based indices into sorted ID lists (docs/mixed-onroad.md §0.1).",
        "esio_format": "parquet"
      }
    },
